                                                                  2431 1451
             New evaluation of chromium isotopes                  2431 1451
                 BNL, ORNL, IAEA - August 2020                    2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
       G.P.A. Nobre, M.T. Pigni, D.A. Brown, R. Capote, A. Trkov, 2431 1451
 K.H. Guber, R. Arcilla, J. Gutierrez, A. Cuadra, G. Arbanas      2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
Resolved Resonance Region:                                        2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
For 52Cr, RRR, defined up to the threshold of the first           2431 1451
inelastic, was taken from ENDF/B-VIII.0, including the DSD        2431 1451
capture background.                                               2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
Angular distributions were reconstructed from resonance           2431 1451
parameters using the Blatt-Biedenharn formalism and then were     2431 1451
minimally smoothed so that their energy dependence could be       2431 1451
represented as faithfully as possible given the limitations of    2431 1451
the ENDF format.                                                  2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
Fast region:                                                      2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
Above the inelastic threshold, the nuclear reaction model         2431 1451
code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta (SVN rev.  5170; source rev.  5168) was   2431 1451
employed. Optical model calculations were performed using the     2431 1451
dispersive soft-rotor optical potential of Li et al. (RIPL #616)  2431 1451
through the OPTMAN module of EMPIRE.                              2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
Generally, fast-range fits followed Abfalterer/Foster Jr. data    2431 1451
for total cross section, total inelastic data and partial         2431 1451
inelastic gamma data of Milhailescu, recent (n,p) data (in        2431 1451
particular the sets from Fessler and Mannhart), and IRDFF (n,2n)  2431 1451
below 20 MeV.                                                     2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
Below 5 MeV, the following modifications were implemented:        2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
- Partial inelastic cross sections below 5 MeV (MT=51) and below  2431 1451
  4 MeV (MT=52,53,54,55) were replaced by Mihailescu experimental 2431 1451
  data. MT=4 and MT=1 were reconstructed accordingly and          2431 1451
  difference was incorporated into the elastic channel.           2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
- Total cross section between 3.6 MeV and 6.0 MeV was replaced    2431 1451
  by experimental data from Perey using natural chromium samples  2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
- Total cross section below 3.6 MeV was replaced by               2431 1451
  experimental data from Carlton taken at 200 flight path         2431 1451
  for Cr-52. In this energy region, resolution-broadened          2431 1451
  Carlton data are consistent with Perey data for natCr.          2431 1451
  The differences in resolution lead to large differences         2431 1451
  in calculated self-shielding corrections below 3 MeV.           2431 1451
  Larger corrections result from the use of Carlton data.         2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
- Elastic cross section defined as the difference between total   2431 1451
  and sum of all non-elastic cross sections.                      2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
- Elastic angular distributions between 1.6 and 2.8 Mev were      2431 1451
  taken from fit of Guenther 82 data, after small tuning to       2431 1451
  increase forward scattering by half the uncertainty. Above      2431 1451
  4.5 MeV, angular distributions are taken directly from EMPIRE.  2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
