 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, November 1989, D. Larson (ORNL)      2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
   This work employed nuclear model codes including the           2431 1451
Distorted Wave Born Approximation (DWBA) program DWUCK [Ku72]     2431 1451
and the Hauser-Feshbach code TNG [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86].  The TNG code  2431 1451
provides energy and angular distributions of particles emitted    2431 1451
in the compound and pre-compound reactions, ensures consistency   2431 1451
among all reactions, and maintains energy balance. Details        2431 1451
pertinent to the contents of this evaluation and extensive        2431 1451
comparisons of calculations with experimental data can be found   2431 1451
in Hetrick [He87].                                                2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
DESCRIPTION OF FILES                                              2431 1451
(MF-MT)                                                           2431 1451
  1-451 GENERAL INFORMATION, REFERENCES, AND DEFINITIONS.         2431 1451
  2-151 RESONANCE PARAMETERS;  USED TO PROVIDE THE TOTAL AND      2431 1451
        SCATTERING CROSS SECTIONS FROM 1.E-5 EV TO 980 KEV, AND   2431 1451
        CAPTURE FROM 1.E-5 TO 375 KEV.  A SMALL CONTRIBUTION IN   2431 1451
        3-102 IS ADDED TO 2-151 FOR CAPTURE FROM 375 TO 980 KEV   2431 1451
        (SEE 3-102 BELOW).  THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS              2431 1451
        FROM [Br85] (WITH HELP FROM BRUSEGAN ET AL. (PRIVATE      2431 1451
        COMM., 1988)) WERE ADJUSTED TO MINIMIZE DIFFERENCE WITH   2431 1451
        DATA OF REF. [Ag84].                                      2431 1451
        NOTE THAT THE FLAG HAS BEEN SET TO ALLOW USER CALCULATION 2431 1451
        OF THE ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS FROM THE R-M RESONANCE       2431 1451
        PARAMETERS, IF THE USER WANTS ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ON    2431 1451
        A FINER ENERGY GRID THAN GIVEN IN 4/2.                    2431 1451
  3-1   TOTAL CROSS SECTION; GIVEN BY RESONANCE PARAMETERS UP TO  2431 1451
        980 KEV WITH NEGATIVE ENERGY RESONANCES ADJUSTED TO GIVE  2431 1451
        MEASURED THERMAL SCATTERING AND CAPTURE CROSS SECTIONS    2431 1451
        (SEE 3-102 BELOW).  FROM 20 - 980 KEV A BACKGROUND FILE   2431 1451
        IS REQUIRED.  FROM 980 KEV TO 20.0 MEV, HIGH              2431 1451
        RESOLUTION NAT CR TRANSMISSION MEASUREMENTS WERE USED     2431 1451
        D.C. LARSON, J.A. HARVEY, AND N.W. HILL, PRIVATE COMM.,   2431 1451
        1988; DATA AVAILABLE AT NNDC) RATHER THAN LOWER           2431 1451
        RESOLUTION ISOTOPIC DATA.                                 2431 1451
  3-2   ELASTIC SCATTERING CROSS SECTIONS WERE OBTAINED BY        2431 1451
        SUBTRACTING THE NONELASTIC FROM THE TOTAL                 2431 1451
  3-3   NONELASTIC CROSS SECTION; SUM OF 3-4, 3-16, 3-22,         2431 1451
        3-28, 3-102, 3-103, AND 3-107.                            2431 1451
  3-4   TOTAL INELASTIC CROSS SECTION; SUM OF 3-51, 3-52, ..      2431 1451
        .., 3-60, AND 3-91                                        2431 1451
  3-16  (N,2N) CROSS SECTIONS WERE TAKEN FROM THE ACTIVATION      2431 1451
        FILE FOR 52CR BUT WERE ADJUSTED TO BE SMALLER             2431 1451
        BELOW ENERGY OF 15.5 MEV TO MATCH THE DATA                2431 1451
        OF WAGNER ET AL. [Wa88] WHICH AGREES WELL WITH OTHER      2431 1451
        DATA IN THIS ENERGY REGION.                               2431 1451
  3-22  (N,NA) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG CODE     2431 1451
        [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86].  NO DATA AVAILABLE OTHER THAN A-EMISSION2431 1451
  3-28  (N,NP) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG CODE     2431 1451
        [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86].  NO DATA AVAILABLE OTHER THAN P-EMISSION2431 1451
  3-51 TO 3-60 INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING LEVELS; RESULTS ARE  2431 1451
        FROM TNG [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86] WHICH INCLUDES DIRECT           2431 1451
        INTERACTION CROSS SECTIONS FROM DWUCK [Ku72] CALCULATIONS.2431 1451
        COMPARISONS  WITH EXPERIMENTAL DATA USED IN THE EVALUATION2431 1451
        PROCESS ARE SHOWN IN [He87].                              2431 1451
  3-91  INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING THE CONTINUUM (TNG          2431 1451
        CALCULATED).  GUIDANCE FROM (N,XN) EMISSION DATA [He87].  2431 1451
  3-102 (N,G) CAPTURE CROSS SECTION; GIVEN BY RESONANCE PARAMETERS2431 1451
        UP TO 980 KEV AND FROM 980 KEV TO 20 MEV, TNG CALC'S      2431 1451
        WERE USED BUT NORMALIZED TO MEASURED AVE. CAPTURE BETWEEN 2431 1451
        100 KEV AND 1.0 MEV.  A SMALL CONTIBUTION TO BE ADDED TO  2431 1451
        2-151 IS GIVEN FROM 375-980 KEV DUE TO INCOMPLETE         2431 1451
        CAPTURE RESONANCE INFORMATION.  TNG CALCULATIONS INCLUDED 2431 1451
        A PRECOMPOUND COMPONENT AND WEIGHTED CROSS SECTIONS FROM  2431 1451
        ISOTOPES OF CR GIVE 0.82 MB AT 14.5 MEV, IN AGREEMENT WITH2431 1451
        THE MEASUREMENT OF 0.75 MB FOR NAT CR.                    2431 1451
  3-103 (N,P) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG CODE      2431 1451
        [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86], BUT MODIFIED BETWEEN 7 TO 16 MEV TO     2431 1451
        BETTER FIT THE DATA OF SMITH ET AL. [Sm80] UP TO 9 MEV AND2431 1451
        RECENT MEASUREMENTS AT 14.5 MEV [Gu85,Ar80,Mo77].         2431 1451
  3-107 (N,A) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG CODE      2431 1451
        [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86]. NO DATA AVAILABLE OTHER THAN A-EMISSION.2431 1451
  4-2   ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY NEUTRONS GIVEN FOR     2431 1451
        ELASTIC SCATTERING ARE FROM ENDF/B-V.                     2431 1451
        IF DESIRED, ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS CAN BE CALCULATED BY    2431 1451
        THE USER ON A FINER ENERGY GRID FROM THE R-M RESONANCE    2431 1451
        PARAMETERS IN 2/151.                                      2431 1451
  6-16  (N,2N) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2431 1451
        NEUTRON AND 51CR RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD     2431 1451
        BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA   2431 1451
        RAY; TNG CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR2431 1451
        EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR    2431 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON).  (N,XN) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY  2431 1451
        USED TO BENCHMARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS [He87].            2431 1451
  6-22  (N,NA) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2431 1451
        NEUTRON, ALPHA, AND 48TI RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT   2431 1451
        YIELD BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE   2431 1451
        GAMMA RAY; CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN  2431 1451
        FOR EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY    2431 1451
        FOR THE OUTGOING NEUTRON; ISOTROPY IS ASSUMED FOR THE     2431 1451
        ALPHA AND RESIDUAL).  (N,XA) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY    2431 1451
        USED TO BENCHMARK THE CALCULATIONS [He87].                2431 1451
  6-28  (N,NP) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2431 1451
        NEUTRON AND 51V RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD      2431 1451
        BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA   2431 1451
        RAY; CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR    2431 1451
        EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR    2431 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON).  (N,XP) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY  2431 1451
        USED TO BENCHMARK THE CALCULATIONS [He87].                2431 1451
  6-51 THROUGH 6-60 INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING LEVELS; EACH    2431 1451
        SECTION INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE NEUTRON   2431 1451
        AND 52CR RESIDUAL; ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR    2431 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON (LEGENDRE COEFFICIENTS COMPUTED      2431 1451
        BY DWUCK [Ku72] AND TNG [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86].  COMPARISONS    2431 1451
        WITH ANGULAR DISTRIBUTION DATA ARE GIVEN IN [He87].       2431 1451
  6-91  INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING THE CONTINUUM; INCLUDES     2431 1451
        SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE NEUTRON AND 52CR           2431 1451
        RESIDUAL AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED ON TNG          2431 1451
        CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA RAY; TNG       2431 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN             2431 1451
        FOR EACH (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR THE    2431 1451
        OUTGOING NEUTRON).  (N,XN) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY USED 2431 1451
        TO BENCHMARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS [He87].                 2431 1451
  6-103 (N,P) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR P     2431 1451
        AND 52V RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED        2431 1451
        ON CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR GAMMA RAY;            2431 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR EACH    2431 1451
        PRODUCT.  (N,XP) D-D EMISSION DATA USED TO BENCHMARK      2431 1451
        THE TNG CALCULATIONS [He87].                              2431 1451
  6-107 (N,A) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR A     2431 1451
        AND 49TI RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED       2431 1451
        ON CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR GAMMA RAY;            2431 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR EACH    2431 1451
        PRODUCT.  (N,XA) D-D EMISSION DATA USED TO BENCHMARK      2431 1451
        THE TNG CALCULATIONS [He87].                              2431 1451
